message: >
  If you use MATH-SYNC, please cite this software release using
  the Zenodo DOI and the metadata in this file.

type: software

title: >
  MATH-SYNC v1.1: Reproducible Computational Pipeline for Robust
  and Identifiable Affine-Clock Alignment of Heterogeneous
  Multirate Sensor Streams

version: "1.1"

date-released: "2026-10-02"

authors:
  - family-names: "Hechavarria-Hernandez"
    given-names: "Jesus Rafael"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9013-8665"
    affiliation: "Universidad ECOTEC"

license: MIT

repository-code: "https://github.com/jrhechavarriah/MATH_SYNC_v1.0"

keywords:
  - clock synchronization
  - temporal alignment
  - affine clock model
  - clock skew
  - robust estimation
  - Huber M-estimation
  - identifiability
  - multirate sensor streams
  - multimodal sensing
  - reproducibility
  - sensitivity analysis
  - computational robustness

abstract: >
  MATH-SYNC v1.1 is a reproducible computational release for robust and
  identifiable affine-clock alignment of heterogeneous multirate sensor
  streams. It preserves the complete frozen v1.0 validation package and adds
  reviewer-driven supplementary robustness analyses covering alternative
  robust estimators, anchor geometry, reference-stream sensitivity, and
  convergence and computational-scaling diagnostics. The release includes
  frozen experiment specifications, Supplementary Tables S2-S5, raw and
  summarized G12 results, automated tests, and SHA-256 integrity metadata.
  The original MATH-SYNC v1.0 validation remains preserved unchanged.

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23106783"

